# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored: CI runs `npm ci`, which needs
# it, and pinning the SDK is only reproducible if the lockfile ships with the
# repo. It stays listed in .dclignore, so it is still kept out of deployments.
*.js
node_modules
bin/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Decentraland AI skills, installed locally with
#   npx skills add decentraland/sdk-skills --all
# ~7 MB of third-party instruction files. They are a developer aid, not part of
# the scene, and shipping them would put someone else's content under our
# licence. Anyone cloning this repo re-runs the command above.
.agents/
.claude/
agent/
skills-lock.json

# Source art. Blender files are large binaries and are not what the scene
# loads — only exported .glb ever belongs in a Decentraland project.
*.blend
*.blend[0-9]*
# Creator Hub leftovers. `.editor/` is local project state, and the
# autogenerated thumbnail is a 588 KB render of the empty editor grid — our
# arena is built in code, so there is nothing in the editor to photograph.
# scene.json points navmapThumbnail at the real image instead.
.editor/
assets/images/autogenerated-thumbnail.png

# Screen recordings and extracted frames from device QA. Large, and evidence
# rather than source — they belong in the conversation, not the repository.
qa/
